> a(x: u4) = x + x
> b(x: u4) = x << 1
> equiv a b
a and b are equal on the domain of a (exhaustive)
> c(x: u8) = (x & 0x0F) + (x xor 0x0F)
> d(x: u8) = (x | 0x0F)
> equiv c d
c and d are equal on the domain of c (exhaustive)
> e(x: u4) = x*3
> f(x: u4) = x*3 + 1
> equiv e f
e and f differ at 16 points, e.g. x=0: 0 vs 1
